#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078187 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078468 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1d905f41-5940-547e-b3d2-558c6b881b68" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Index of a Term in an Arithmetic Sequence"}] :question/id #uuid "eec455b0-98ff-59a5-b552-3381fb893fd2" :question/math-academy-id "e-14392" :question/problem "What is the index of the term $42$ in the following arithmetic sequence?\n\n$$\n-10, \\: -6, \\: -2, \\: \\ldots\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Since $a_1=-10$ and \n\n$$\nd=-6-(-10)=4,\n$$\n\nwe can construct the formula for the $n$th term as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}+(n-1)d \\\\  & =-10+(n-1)(4) \\\\  & =-10+4n-4 \\\\  & =4n-14\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve for the value of $n$ that gives $a_n=42,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & =4n-14 \\\\ 42 & =4n-14 \\\\ 56 & =4n \\\\ 14 & =n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $42$ is the $14$th term of the sequence."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078188 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078469 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3c61d587-2441-5e8c-8da1-5bd62ff98e1e" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Index of a Term Given the Recursive Formula"}] :question/id #uuid "ff198a0e-d34e-5706-ad74-dbfa20fc3a94" :question/math-academy-id "e-14395" :question/problem "Given the arithmetic sequence\n\n$$\na_{n+1} = a_n + 12, \\quad a_1 = 3,\\quad n\\geq 1,\n$$\n\nwhat is the index of the term $255?$" :question/worked-solution "We will convert the recursive formula to an explicit formula and then solve for the value of $n$ such that $a_n=255.$\n\nThe recursive rule for an arithmetic sequence takes the form\n\n$$\na_{n+1} = a_n +{\\color{black}d}.\n$$\n\nIn the given formula, we have $d={\\color{black}12}.$ We are also told that $a_1={\\color{black}3},$ so we can write the explicit formula as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}+(n-1)d \\\\  & =3+(n-1)(12) \\\\  & =3+12n-12 \\\\  & =12n-9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve for the value of $n$ such that $a_n=255\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & =12n-9 \\\\ 255 & =12n-9 \\\\ 264 & =12n \\\\ \\frac{264}{12} & =n \\\\ 22 & =n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $255$ is the $22$nd term of the sequence."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078189 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078470 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2bbbc551-e3ff-5cce-a572-e5b89067005a" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Index of a Term Given Another Term and the Common Difference"}] :question/id #uuid "84266116-5a1b-528a-929a-40b5d863e5a5" :question/math-academy-id "e-14397" :question/problem "Given an arithmetic sequence that has $a_4=5$ and common difference $d=3$, what is the index of the term $95?$" :question/worked-solution "Since $a_4=5$ is $3$ jumps after $a_1,$ we can determine the first term of the sequence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{4} & ={a}_{1}+3d \\\\ 5 & ={a}_{1}+3(3) \\\\ 5 & ={a}_{1}+9 \\\\ -4 & ={a}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the formula for the $n$th term is:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}+(n-1)d \\\\  & =-4+(n-1)(3) \\\\  & =-4+3n-3 \\\\  & =3n-7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve for the value of $n$ that gives $a_n=95,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & =3n-7 \\\\ 95 & =3n-7 \\\\ 102 & =3n \\\\ \\frac{102}{3} & =n \\\\ 34 & =n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $95$ is the $34$th term of the sequence."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078191 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078471 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d979a7bd-42a1-5d4f-8717-1caa06ce623c" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Index of a Term Given Two Terms"}] :question/id #uuid "5b905b18-5ac3-5a0f-a42f-1d9e53e792cc" :question/math-academy-id "e-14399" :question/problem "Given an arithmetic sequence that has $a_2=12$ and $a_{4} = 10$, what is the index of the term $-12?$" :question/worked-solution "To construct the formula for the sequence, we need to know the common difference $d$ and the first term $a_1.$\n\nSince we are given $a_2=12$ and $a_4=10,$ we can find the common difference by dividing the total difference by the number of jumps:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =\\frac{{a}_{4}-{a}_{2}}{4-2} \\\\  & =\\frac{10-12}{4-2} \\\\  & =\\frac{-2}{2} \\\\  & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $a_2=12$ is $1$ jump after $a_1,$ we can determine the first term of the sequence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{2} & ={a}_{1}+d \\\\ 12 & ={a}_{1}-1 \\\\ 13 & ={a}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the formula for the $n$th term is:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}+(n-1)d \\\\  & =13+(n-1)(-1) \\\\  & =14-n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we solve for the value of $n$ that gives $a_n=-12,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & =14-n \\\\ -12 & =14-n \\\\ -26 & =-n \\\\ 26 & =n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $-12$ is the $26$th term of the sequence."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186560981 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078469 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3c61d587-2441-5e8c-8da1-5bd62ff98e1e" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Index of a Term Given the Recursive Formula"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "19cb2987-9eb4-54be-b08e-162c5813a545" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "17" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560424} {:answer/id #uuid "9ad4665b-2a16-57dc-98b1-8b2332bc6345" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "42" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560679} {:answer/id #uuid "d77a9cbb-50ff-5df0-b6ea-7d7f8d699e44" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "23" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560789} {:answer/id #uuid "e5c2b468-a6ef-5eb8-85d2-1cac557ffbd5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "19" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560811} {:answer/id #uuid "ee5b6310-950b-55c9-97bc-4b58e773901a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "31" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560829}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "19cb2987-9eb4-54be-b08e-162c5813a545" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "17" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560424} :answer-field/id #uuid "59c55c39-31ed-5a5f-b3f0-661161fb6320" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560900}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "20db0785-68d0-5682-b7db-691770b91085" :question/math-academy-id "q-101056" :question/problem "What is the index of the term $24$ for the arithmetic sequence below?\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+1}={a}_{n}+2,\\,{a}_{1}=-8,\\,n\\ge 1\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We will convert the recursive formula to an explicit formula and then solve for the value of $n$ such that ${a}_{n}=24.$\n\nThe recursive rule for an arithmetic sequence takes the form\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+1}={a}_{n}+d.\n$$\n\nIn the given formula, we have $d=2.$ We are also told that ${a}_{1}=-8,$ so we can write the explicit formula as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}+(n-1)d \\\\  & =-8+(n-1)(2) \\\\  & =-8+2n-2 \\\\  & =2n-10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve for the value of $n$ such that ${a}_{n}=24:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & =2n-10 \\\\ 24 & =2n-10 \\\\ 34 & =2n \\\\ \\frac{34}{2} & =n \\\\ 17 & =n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $24$ is the $17$th term of the sequence."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561039 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078471 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d979a7bd-42a1-5d4f-8717-1caa06ce623c" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Index of a Term Given Two Terms"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "087e33e7-ce0a-5e16-99c0-73c8c4b7df67" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "25" :db/id #edb/ref 1