n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{3} & ={a}_{1}+2d \\\\ 21 & ={a}_{1}+2(3) \\\\ 21 & ={a}_{1}+6 \\\\ 15 & ={a}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the formula for the $n$th term is:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}+(n-1)d \\\\  & =15+(n-1)(3) \\\\  & =15+3n-3 \\\\  & =3n+12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve for the value of $n$ that gives ${a}_{n}=108,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & =3n+12 \\\\ 108 & =3n+12 \\\\ 96 & =3n \\\\ \\frac{96}{3} & =n \\\\ 32 & =n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $108$ is the $32$nd term of the sequence."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561021 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078468 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1d905f41-5940-547e-b3d2-558c6b881b68" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Index of a Term in an Arithmetic Sequence"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "28eac1df-eb17-5a8c-b1d6-e7763ffbd108" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "50" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560452}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "28eac1df-eb17-5a8c-b1d6-e7763ffbd108" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "50" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560452} :answer-field/id #uuid "e49d3c25-3f4f-563e-b4f2-136b5e9bc6c2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560960}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "86d5fb73-7ead-50e4-a1b1-3981ab0d7b12" :question/math-academy-id "q-214192" :question/problem "Given the arithmetic sequence ${a}_{n}=3n-4$ for $n\\ge 1,$ the index of the term $146$ is\n\n$n=$\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Using the formula for the $n$th term of an arithmetic sequence, we solve for the value of $n$ that gives ${a}_{n}=146$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & =3n-4 \\\\ 146 & =3n-4 \\\\ 150 & =3n \\\\ 50 & =n \\\\ n & =50\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $146$ is the $50$th term of the sequence."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078780 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078469 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3c61d587-2441-5e8c-8da1-5bd62ff98e1e" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Index of a Term Given the Recursive Formula"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d3d280e7-fa4b-57c4-93a1-05e210a04c35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "22" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560785}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d3d280e7-fa4b-57c4-93a1-05e210a04c35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "22" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560785} :answer-field/id #uuid "31aeabda-61fa-58f0-a30e-ee7377fc5759" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186075711}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "cd8712dc-cbd7-5694-8112-15a3c2418d2d" :question/math-academy-id "q-214198" :question/problem "Given the arithmetic sequence \n\n$$\n{a}_{n+1}={a}_{n}-6,\\,{a}_{1}=2,\\,n\\ge 1,\n$$\n\nthe index of the term $-124$ is $n=${{field-1}}." :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "We will convert the recursive formula to an explicit formula and then solve for the value of $n$ such that ${a}_{n}=-124.$\n\nThe recursive rule for an arithmetic sequence takes the form\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+1}={a}_{n}+d.\n$$\n\nIn the given formula, we have $d=-6.$ We are also told that ${a}_{1}=2,$ so we can write the explicit formula as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}+(n-1)d \\\\  & =2+(n-1)(-6) \\\\  & =2-6n+6 \\\\  & =-6n+8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve for the value of $n$ such that ${a}_{n}=-124:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & =-6n+8 \\\\ -124 & =-6n+8 \\\\ -132 & =-6n \\\\ \\frac{-132}{-6} & =n \\\\ 22 & =n \\\\ n & =22\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $-124$ is the $22$nd term of the sequence."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078781 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078471 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d979a7bd-42a1-5d4f-8717-1caa06ce623c" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Index of a Term Given Two Terms"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "19bfa584-f587-57a2-b974-c46d9079b18d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560423}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "19bfa584-f587-57a2-b974-c46d9079b18d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560423} :answer-field/id #uuid "60026508-8aeb-53d1-b9a9-b02a4098935f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186075712}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "34bf3da3-eeb6-5d73-91c4-1ece08cbe280" :question/math-academy-id "q-214239" :question/problem "If an arithmetic sequence has ${a}_{6}=12$ and ${a}_{9}=24$, find the value of $n$ such that ${a}_{n}=132.$\n\n$n=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "To construct the formula for the sequence, we need to know the common difference $d$ and the first term ${a}_{1}.$\n\nSince we are given ${a}_{6}=12$ and ${a}_{9}=24,$ we can find the common difference by dividing the total difference by the number of jumps:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =\\frac{{a}_{9}-{a}_{6}}{9-6} \\\\  & =\\frac{24-12}{9-6} \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{3} \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since ${a}_{6}=12$ is $5$ jumps after ${a}_{1},$ we can determine the first term of the sequence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{6} & ={a}_{1}+5d \\\\ 12 & ={a}_{1}+5(4) \\\\ 12 & ={a}_{1}+20 \\\\ -8 & ={a}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the formula for the $n$th term is:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}+(n-1)d \\\\  & =-8+(n-1)(4) \\\\  & =-8+4n-4 \\\\  & =4n-12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve for the value of $n$ that gives ${a}_{n}=132,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & =4n-12 \\\\ 132 & =4n-12 \\\\ 144 & =4n \\\\ n & =\\frac{144}{4} \\\\ n & =36\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $132$ is the $36$th term of the sequence."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186560983 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078470 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2bbbc551-e3ff-5cce-a572-e5b89067005a" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Index of a Term Given Another Term and the Common Difference"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "54903364-fc3c-52cf-a100-0884cb95a8c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560548} {:answer/id #uuid "56f8a9a0-032d-5cd7-8aed-1b6cfb55879f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560552} {:answer/id #uuid "ca9e0a2d-3a3e-5174-9c47-74cae73ba479" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560769} {:answer/id #uuid "dff856d3-22d9-59a1-8645-6d200dedd454" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560806} {:answer/id #uuid "ff93aca6-55a3-5d95-8cf9-365d68157668" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560864}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dff856d3-22d9-59a1-8645-6d200dedd454" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560806} :answer-field/id #uuid "30f7986d-cac2-551c-bff5-9034f82065ce" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560881}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "293ef266-e6e1-5fbe-bca3-98219ac748f8" :question/math-academy-id "q-236074" :question/problem "Given an arithmetic sequence that has $f(11)=78$ and common difference $d=4$, what is the index of the term $50?$" :question/worked-solution "Since $f(11)=78$ is $10$ jumps after $f(1),$ we can determine the first term of the sequence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(11) & =f(1)+10d \\\\ 78 & =f(1)+10(4) \\\\ 78 & =f(1)+40 \\\\ 38 & =f(1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the formula for the $n$th term is:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(n) & =f(1)+(n-1)d \\\\  & =38+(n-1)(4) \\\\  & =38+4n-4 \\\\  & =4n+34\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve for the value of $n$ that gives $f(n)=50,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(n) & =4n+34 \\\\ 50 & =4n+34 \\\\ 16 & =4n \\\\ \\frac{16}{4} & =n \\\\ 4 & =n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $50$ is the $4$th term of the sequence."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186560979 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078468 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1d905f41-5940-547e-b3d2-558c6b881b68" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Index of a Term in an Arithmetic Sequence"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "97ce1c4d-1ed0-52c4-a1e7-0c3b7ba3d2d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "90" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560673}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "97ce1c4d-1ed0-52c4-a1e7-0c3b7ba3d2d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "90" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560673} :answer-field/id #uuid "bf63bf8f-0363-542c-979e-31d561484307" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560948}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1e26006d-428f-5619-b63c-23ae2341e3ff" :question/math-academy-id "q-236399" :question/problem "Given the arithmetic sequence ${a}_{n}=100-8n$ for $n\\ge 1,$ the index of the term $-620$ is\n\n$n=$\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Using the formula for the $n$th term of an arithmetic sequence, we solve for the value of $n$ that gives ${a}_{n}=-620$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & =100-8n \\\\ -620 & =100-8n \\\\ 8n & =720 \\\\ n & =90\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $-620$ is the $90$th term of the sequence."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561051 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078470 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2bbbc551-e3ff-5cce-a572-e5b89067005a" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Index of a Term Given Another Term and the Common Difference"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "21caf3d6-5a6d-5230-b9a3-457061878b3c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "51" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560441}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "21caf3d6-5a6d-5230-b9a3-457061878b3c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "51" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560441} :answer-field/id #uuid "74bbf873-fee2-5e1e-acd8-4366a8ef81bf" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560912}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d33dfdeb-3e95-57f8-81f1-41fd9826c2ae" :question/math-academy-id "q-236846" :question/problem "If an arithmetic sequence has $f(15)=-4$ and common difference $d=-5$, find the value of $n$ such that $f(n)=-184.$\n\n$\\,n=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Since $f(15)=-4$ is $14$ jumps after $f(1),$ we can determine the first term of the sequence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(15) & =f(1)+14d \\\\ -4 & =f(1)+14(-5) \\\\ -4 & =f(1)-70 \\\\ 66 & =f(1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the formula for the $n$th term is:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(n) & =f(1)+(n-1)d \\\\  & =66+(n-1)(-5) \\\\  & =66-5n+5 \\\\  & =71-5n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve for the value of $n$ that gives $f(n)=-184,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(n) & =71-5n \\\\ -184 & =71-5n \\\\ -255 & =-5n \\\\ n & =\\frac{-255}{-5} \\\\ n & =51\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $-184$ is the $51$st term of the sequence."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561050 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078468 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1d905f41-5940-547e-b3d2-558c6b881b68" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Index of a Term in an Arithmetic Sequence"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0503b0d3-7253-51fa-aab8-783b239ef61f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560371} {:answer/id #uuid "22df1e8f-0e2a-5fab-aa0b-9c1e92c70910" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560445} {:answer/id #uuid "aa5b8fef-1b13-51b2-a03c-72cd58df636e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "19" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560706} {:answer/id #uuid "e675d5e6-6517-53b9-9ccf-ccab622056a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "23" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560813} {:answer/id #uuid "eee5ed79-f0b2-5d1a-a548-0aa6036f9d5c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "27" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560831}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e675d5e6-6517-53b9-9ccf-ccab622056a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "23" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560813} :answer-field/id #uuid "47e54f65-1c66-57bb-9be2-d1f8e1c2752f" :answer-field/key "s